Third-party software
--------------------
The cloudseed repository does not vendor third-party source code. The CLI
(cloudseed/) uses only the Python standard library. The following are fetched
at build or run time, each under its own license:

  * providers/vmdesktop (cloudseed's Terraform provider for VMware Fusion /
    Workstation) is compiled against HashiCorp's terraform-plugin-framework and
    its dependencies (see providers/vmdesktop/go.mod and go.sum), mostly under
    the Mozilla Public License 2.0, BSD-style and Apache-2.0 licenses.
  * Terraform, the cloud providers' Terraform providers, Ansible, the cloud
    CLIs, kubectl, Helm, k9s and the other tools that `cloudseed install` or
    `cloudseed deps` download or that the Dockerfile builds into an image.
    The single-binary bundle (`cloudseed deps bundle`) embeds a Terraform
    release; Terraform is distributed by HashiCorp under the Business Source
    License 1.1, so check its terms before redistributing a bundle.
  * The Helm charts and manifests installed by `cloudseed platform install`
    (the platform catalog in cloudseed/platform.py). They are pulled from their
    upstream repositories and remain under their authors' licenses.
  * The built-in agent installs the Anthropic Python SDK into its own virtual
    environment on first use (~/.cloudseed/venv-agent).
  * Official cloud images (Ubuntu, Debian) that `cloudseed setup vmware`
    downloads are subject to their distributors' terms.

